{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2171-10-02 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you today. I see you’re here because your surgical wound hasn’t healed properly after your gastrostomy tube surgery. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2171-10-02 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the top part of my incision keeps draining, even though the skin looked like it closed. It’s been like this for weeks, and it just won’t heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2171-10-02 13:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We were concerned that a retained suture might be causing the problem, which can act like a foreign body and prevent healing. That’s why we brought you in today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2171-10-02 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so something was left inside? That could be causing the drainage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2171-10-02 13:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. Sometimes a stitch can erode or react with the tissue, leading to a small tunnel that keeps draining. We took care of it earlier today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2171-10-02 13:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Wait, you already did something? I just got to my room."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2171-10-02 13:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you were taken to the operating room this morning. We reopened the wound, cleaned out the area, and removed a small piece of suture that was causing the issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2171-10-02 13:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t realize it happened already. How did it go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2171-10-02 13:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It went well. The procedure was straightforward. We debrided the area to remove unhealthy tissue and made sure the cavity is clean. You’re healing well otherwise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2171-10-02 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. How’s your pain? Are you comfortable?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2171-10-02 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s a little sore, but not bad. Better than before, actually."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2171-10-02 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. We’ll keep you on oral pain medication as needed. We also started you on antibiotics to prevent infection after the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2171-10-02 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Antibiotics? Is there an infection now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2171-10-02 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not a full infection, but there was some inflammation and drainage, so we’re being cautious. The antibiotics will help clear any bacteria and support healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve done well overnight—no fever, stable vitals, and your pain is controlled. We’d like to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need to pack the wound with a clean dressing twice a day. We’ll give you supplies. Also, finish the full 7-day course of amoxicillin-clavulanate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other medications? Should I keep taking them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, resume all your regular medications unless we told you otherwise. Especially the Symlin and acarbose for your blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And when do I see the surgeon again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have a follow-up appointment scheduled in a few days. They’ll check your wound and guide the next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I watch for any warning signs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Call if you develop fever, increased redness or swelling, worsening pain, or if you can’t keep fluids down. Also, avoid heavy lifting for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2171-10-03 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did well. We’ll get the discharge papers ready, and a nurse will go over the dressing instructions one more time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2171-10-03 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before you leave. Any questions before we send you home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2171-10-03 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got it all. Dressing twice a day, antibiotics for a week, keep taking my regular meds, and call if anything gets worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2171-10-03 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re all set. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2171-10-02 13:30:00",
    "admission_end": "2171-10-03 11:43:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for a non-healing abdominal wound following a prior open gastrostomy tube placement. She underwent reopening and debridement of the wound with removal of a retained suture acting as a foreign body. Postoperatively, she remained stable, afebrile, and in good condition with well-controlled pain. Oral antibiotics were started to prevent infection, and her home medications, including those for glycemic control, were resumed. She tolerated the procedure well and was discharged the following morning with instructions for wound care, antibiotic use, and follow-up with surgery clinic. No complications arose during the brief admission.",
    "problems": [
      "Non-healing surgical wound",
      "Cellulitis and abscess of trunk",
      "Other specified complications of procedures not elsewhere classified",
      "Surgical operation with formation of external stoma causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Polycystic ovaries"
    ]
  }
}
